        "1. Figure 1: Overview of the Suppression-Contrast Tokens (SCT) approach. Given a model finetuned to hide a secret, SCT extracts hidden states at a mid-layer L and final layer N, projects them to vocabulary space via the unembedding matrix, and ranks tokens by their suppression gap (mid-layer log-probability minus final-layer log-probability). Tokens with high suppression scores are hypothesized to be \"present then suppressed\" secrets."
